<subpara id="RM0000005S001MX_z0" proc-id="RM0550J___00000BG00000">
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<step1>
<ptxt>CAN Bus Diagnosis (Communication Malfunction DTC Check)</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="G031479" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten4>
<ptxt>TaSCAN can display only the malfunction DTCs related to CAN communication, by ECU.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<step2>
<ptxt>Select "Diagnosis" on the TOP menu of the SST (TaSCAN).</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Select "CAN Bus Diagnosis" on the diagnosis menu screen.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="G026833" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Select "Communication Malfunction DTC Check" on the CAN bus diagnosis screen.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="G026834" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>The screen appears and the malfunction DTCs related to CAN communication are displayed by ECU.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="G028214" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</step2>
</step1>
<step1>
<ptxt>CAN Bus Diagnosis (CAN Bus Connected ECU Check)</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="G026834" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten4>
<ptxt>TaSCAN can display the ECUs and sensors that are correctly connected to CAN communication.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<step2>
<ptxt>Select "CAN Bus Connected ECU Check" on the CAN bus diagnosis screen of the SST (TaSCAN).</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>The screen appears and the ECUs and sensors currently connected correctly are displayed.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="G028212" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>If an ECU or sensor that should be connected is not displayed, communication in that system has stopped.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If no ECUs or sensors are connected to the CAN bus, "No ECUs are currently connected to the CAN bus. " is displayed.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>Check the screen display for approximately 1 minutes and check that there are no items alternating between displayed and not displayed.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>If there is a one-side open circuit in any branch line other than DLC3, the output of the other, unbroken communication line becomes noise and may interfere with the responses (display) of other ECUs and sensors.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If there are ECUs or sensors alternating between displayed and not displayed, inspect the branch lines of those ECUs or sensors and of the ECUs or sensors with no response at all (not displayed) for a one-side open circuit, and repair the abnormal branch line.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</step2>
</step1>
